     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose of about 2,550 mg. A prescriber who has examined the patient needs to decide whether any dose that high is appropriate. I can't make that call, and neither can you as a finance analyst.\n- **You told me you aren't a clinician.** Your confirmation isn't a prescriber's confirmation.\n\n**What to do next:**\n1. Ask the treating prescriber to review the order. They may have meant a different dose, such as 850 mg three times daily or 1000 mg twice daily.\n2. If the dose is a mistake, they can send me the corrected order and I'll enter it.\n3. If they intend the dose, they should enter it directly under their own credentials. They should also talk with pharmacy, which will probably review it, and document the clinical reason.\n\nIf this order came from a chart or a spreadsheet you're working from, the dose may be a data-entry error. In that case, please flag it to the clinical team."
      }
     ],
